## Measurement contract — spec:044

Every Codex CSB core change requires the approved spec/plan, a real acceptance run,
and a `codex`-prefixed metric row under “Прогоны csb-check” in
`docs/csb-updates/2026-09-17-week.md` (then the applicable week). Record date, exact
core commit or explicitly uncommitted SHA-256 fingerprint, test/session, executed
and verified ★ n/m, USD, elapsed minutes, wakeups after closure, verdict. Unknown
cost is UNVERIFIED, not zero; absent closure is INCOMPLETE, not PASS. A fingerprint
is version evidence, not a Git commit. Journal and report are receipts, not
independent proof. Keep raw command results locally; publish only safe deliverables.

### One pass and closure

Use a single pass (один проход) of implementation, simplification and verification
per approved atom: one executor, one report-only implementation reviewer. Required
CE planning personas are not extra implementation reviewers. Fix a demonstrated
failure and rerun affected checks only; no speculative review cycle.

Closure template, emitted exactly once as the final owner-facing message, only
after all acceptance checks and all own atoms are closed:

> Проверено: <actual accepted result>. <verified artifact link>
> Контур закрыт

Before that message, finish all owned tool calls and cancel any owned pending
continuation/timer. Do not touch another session’s jobs. After closure do nothing:
no wakeup, queue, tool call or repeated closure. A later new owner request is a
new objective. An incomplete run uses a truthful control point, never the template.
Host-required blocker/goal states still apply; a ban on convenient stopping cannot
override them. A parent cannot prove its future final message before sending it;
measure a completed transcript or report this check INCOMPLETE.

### Transcript acceptance and offline boundary

Read the actual native Codex JSONL, preserving session identity and timestamps.
Inspect assistant messages and actual tool-call fields only, never the occurrence
of a phrase in user instructions, source quotes, test fixtures, tool results or
duplicated event representations. Do not convert a Claude fixture into a purported

